  "title": "Verbs",
  "emoji": "🏃",
  "parentNote": "Verbs are action words! Play a fun game: say an action (jump, eat, sleep) and have your child act it out. Also practice \"is, am, are\" — these are helping verbs that are equally important!",
  "learnBullets": [
    "What a **verb** is — a word that shows an action or a state of being",
    "**Action verbs**: run, eat, jump, read, write, play",
    "**Helping verbs**: is, am, are, was, were",
    "Using the right verb form with different subjects"
  ],
  "learnItFirst": "**What is a Verb?**\nA verb is a **doing word** or **action word**. It tells us what someone or something is doing.\n\n```\nThe bird flies. (flies = action)\nI eat breakfast. (eat = action)\nShe is happy. (is = state of being)\n```\n\n**Two Types of Verbs:**\n\n| Type | What it does | Examples |\n|------|-------------|----------|\n| Action verb | Shows an action | run, jump, eat, drink, read, write, sleep, play |\n| Helping verb | Helps the main verb | is, am, are, was, were, has, have |\n\n**Using is, am, are:**\n| Subject | Helping Verb | Example |\n|---------|--------------|---------|\n| I | am | I **am** a student. |\n| He/She/It | is | She **is** happy. |\n| You/We/They | are | They **are** playing. |\n\n### 🧠 How to Find a Verb — 3 Easy Steps\n1. **Ask:** What is the person or thing doing?\n2. **Check:** Can you act it out? (run, jump, eat, sleep)\n3. **Look:** Is there a \"be\" verb? (is, am, are)\n\n---",
